---
// ScreenLingo support page. App Store Connect uses this as the Support URL, so keep it stable.
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { withBase } from '../../lib/url';

const contact = 'xinzhao.dev@gmail.com';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="ScreenLingo"
  description="ScreenLingo translates German or Dutch apps on your phone with one double-tap on the back. Everything stays on the device."
>
  <article class="prose">
    <header class="page-head">
      <h1>ScreenLingo</h1>
      <p class="muted">
        Read German or Dutch apps in English or Chinese. Double-tap the back of your phone and
        ScreenLingo shows the same screen, translated.
      </p>
    </header>

    <p>
      Text recognition and translation both run on the device, with Apple's Vision and Translation
      frameworks. You can start without an account, and your screenshots stay on your phone.{' '}
      <a href={withBase('/screenlingo/privacy/')}>Privacy policy</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Setup</h2>
    <p>The app walks you through this on first launch. It takes about two minutes, once.</p>
    <ol>
      <li>Choose your languages and download Apple's language pack (needs network once).</li>
      <li>
        Add the ScreenLingo shortcut (<em>Take Screenshot</em>, then <em>Translate Screen</em>).
      </li>
      <li>
        Open <strong>Settings → Accessibility → Touch → Back Tap → Double Tap</strong> and choose
        <strong>ScreenLingo</strong>.
      </li>
      <li>Double-tap the back of your phone on the guide's example screen to check it works.</li>
    </ol>
    <p>
      Without Back Tap you can still take a screenshot and open it with{' '}
      <em>Translate a screenshot from Photos</em>.
    </p>

    <h2>Questions</h2>
    <h3>Nothing happens when I double-tap.</h3>
    <p>
      Check that Back Tap → Double Tap is set to the ScreenLingo shortcut, and that the shortcut
      contains <em>Take Screenshot</em> and then <em>Translate Screen</em>. Back Tap can miss taps
      through thick cases.
    </p>
    <h3>It says the language isn't downloaded.</h3>
    <p>
      Open ScreenLingo and tap <em>Download</em> next to your language pair. iOS downloads the pack
      from Apple once; after that, translating works offline.
    </p>
    <h3>The screenshot is blank.</h3>
    <p>
      Some apps (banking, video) block screenshots. iOS then delivers a blank image and there is
      nothing to translate.
    </p>
    <h3>A translation is wrong.</h3>
    <p>
      Apple Translation translates each piece of text on its own, so short labels can lose context.
      Tap the list button to see the original and the translation side by side.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions, bugs or ideas: <a href={`mailto:${contact}`}>{contact}</a>
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
